<title>LUXEMBOURG: De Silguy sees no threat to EMU timetable.</title>
<headline>De Silguy sees no threat to EMU timetable.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Monetary Affairs Commissioner Yves-Thibault de Silguy said on Monday that a French request for time to study the EMU budget pact did not threaten the target date for the single currency.</p>
<p>&quot;There is firm commitment to respect the timetable,&quot; he said at a European finance ministers' meeting.  </p>
<p>Earlier, France said it wanted more time to review the stability pact, an agreement by EU countries to ensure budgets do not balloon after the introduction of the EU's single currency.</p>
</text>
